{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:Observations.NVBringAction","@type":"LeanModule","name":"Observations.NVBringAction","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Algebra.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.GroupTheory.SpecificGroups.Alternating","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.rescale_EW_eq_120","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.rescale_EW_eq_120","kind":"theorem","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/n-v-bring-action.lean#L127-L148","doc":"**Corollary.** The rescaling factor at the EW slice equals 120\nwhenever the Markov co-Casimir trace at that slice is nonzero.\n\nThis isolates the structural content of `s5_acts_on_ew_slice`:\nthe `|S_5| = 120` factor is a *property of the rescaling*,\nindependent of the trace's particular value.  Cancellation\nrequires `tau_M_C_dim_q_EW slice ≠ 0`, which holds at generic q\nby the non-degeneracy of the canonical Jones-Markov trace\n(`prop:markov-trace-frobenius-selection`).\n\nConditional on `[NVBringAction slice]` (§3b-cond item 2), not on a\nglobal axiom: divide the class field by `tau_M_C_dim_q_EW slice`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.NVBringAction.rescale_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.NVBringAction.rescale_eq","kind":"theorem","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/n-v-bring-action.lean#L124-L124","doc":"Rescaling identity: $\\tau_{M,C}^{\\mathrm{EW}}(\\Sigma) \\cdot\n\\mathrm{rescale}_{EW}(\\Sigma) = 120 \\cdot\n\\tau_{M,C}^{\\mathrm{EW}}(\\Sigma)$. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.NVBringAction.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.NVBringAction.mk","kind":"ctor","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/n-v-bring-action.lean#L120-L120","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.NVBringAction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.NVBringAction","kind":"class","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/n-v-bring-action.lean#L92-L125","doc":"**`conj:n-v-bring-action` (axiomatised as a typeclass).**\n\nThe §3b-cond carrier: downstream blocks take `[NVBringAction slice]`\nas a typeclass hypothesis and are then genuinely conditional on it.\n\n**There is deliberately NO instance.** Until 2026-09-03 this file also\ncarried `axiom s5_acts_on_ew_slice` together with\n\n    instance instance_from_axiom (slice) : NVBringAction slice where\n      rescale_eq := s5_acts_on_ew_slice slice\n\nand that combination defeated the whole point of the class: instance\nresolution supplies the hypothesis silently, so a downstream author who\nsimply omits `[NVBringAction slice]` gets an axiom-backed theorem whose\n*statement is identical* to the conditional one. Measured on two\ntheorems with the same statement, one written each way:\n\n    downstream_conditional   -> [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]\n    downstream_unconditional -> [..., QOU.Observations.s5_acts_on_ew_slice]\n\nAGENTS.md §3b-tax: \"An unproved primary is honestly represented by a\ncontent-bearing class with NO instance (the open state); do not\nfabricate a trivial instance to 'close' it.\" A global instance\ndischarging the class from a global axiom is exactly that fabrication,\nso both are gone and the file is now axiom-free. Constructing a genuine\ninstance — deriving the S_5 action rather than assuming it — is the open\nwork (bean `qou-5lib`). ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:n-v-bring-action","label":"conj:n-v-bring-action","md":"quantum-observable-universe/observations/n-v-bring-action.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.rescale_EW","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.rescale_EW","kind":"opaque","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/n-v-bring-action.lean#L44-L47","doc":"The categorical Markov-trace-residual rescaling factor that\nconverts the universal Frobenius co-Casimir trace into the\nEW-scale invariant `N_v / q_0^L`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.tau_M_C_dim_q_EW","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.tau_M_C_dim_q_EW","kind":"opaque","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/n-v-bring-action.lean#L40-L42","doc":"The Frobenius co-Casimir trace at the EW slice (the\n`Σ_λ 1/dim_q(λ)` value restricted to the EW Wedderburn blocks). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.tau_M_EW","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.tau_M_EW","kind":"opaque","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/n-v-bring-action.lean#L37-L38","doc":"The Markov trace on `HeckeAtEW`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.HeckeAtEW","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.HeckeAtEW","kind":"opaque","line":31,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/n-v-bring-action.lean#L31-L35","doc":"The Iwahori-Hecke algebra restricted to the EW slice.\nAbstract handle; the concrete `H_{n_EW}(q)` algebra is the\nWedderburn restriction of the universal `H_n(q)` to the\nWedderburn blocks supporting the EW gauge content. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.ElectroweakSlice","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.ElectroweakSlice","kind":"opaque","line":24,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/n-v-bring-action.lean#L24-L29","doc":"The electroweak slice of the brane tower.\nCurrently abstract: a level of the GB filtration / jet order\nat which the weak scale v emerges.  Concrete identification\npending paper-side construction (see\n`conj:mass-endomorphism` for the underlying tower). ","signatureChunk":0}]}